# Commit VNR plan and checklist changes (preserve history)

If anything pivots — scope, approach, hypotheses, stage ordering, or a kill-criterion fires — update BOTH [docs/vnr-build-test-plan.md](../../docs/vnr-build-test-plan.md) and [docs/vnr-checklist.md](../../docs/vnr-checklist.md) to match.

Every change to the plan or the checklist must be saved in a git commit, so the decision history is always recoverable:

- Make plan/checklist edits in a dedicated commit (or alongside the work that caused the pivot), never amend away prior plan history.
- Write the commit body to explain the *why* of the pivot, not just the *what*.
- Do not rewrite or force-push history that contains plan/checklist evolution.

Example commit message:

```
plan: defer TRM baseline to cloud (Stage 0 pivot)

TRM full ARC-AGI-1 training needs ~4 H100s for ~3 days; not feasible on
the local 8 GB GPU. CompressARC becomes the runnable Stage 0 baseline.
```
